  "title": "BigP3BCI Study F — 6x6 multi-paradigm, 3 sessions (10 healthy subjects)",
  "description": "This dataset is Study F of the bigP3BCI collection, a P300-based brain-computer interface speller dataset. It contains 16-channel EEG recorded at 256 Hz over three sessions per subject from 10 participants using a 6x6 character grid with multiple stimulus paradigms. Target and non-target events are annotated with HED tags. The data is a BIDS-formatted derivative of the PhysioNet bigP3BCI release, prepared through MOABB.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a g.USBamp (g.tec) amplifier from 16 channels placed in a standard 10-20 montage, sampled at 256 Hz. Participants performed a P300 speller task with a 6x6 grid and received online feedback. Calibration data were followed by test data.",
